# dwm

Personal build of [dwm](https://dwm.suckless.org/) 6.8, a small dynamic window manager for X.

This tree was copied from the upstream repository, [git.suckless.org/dwm](https://git.suckless.org/dwm). dwm was created by [Anselm R. Garbe](https://garbe.ca/). It is maintained by the [suckless](https://suckless.org/) community, currently by Hiltjo Posthuma. The original code stays under the MIT/X license in `LICENSE`. Thank you for making a window manager that is small enough to read and change.

The status bar uses [slstatus](https://tools.suckless.org/slstatus/), also from suckless: [git.suckless.org/slstatus](https://git.suckless.org/slstatus).

## What this build adds

- Super is the modifier. Alt is only used to launch programs.
- Terminal is qterminal. Super+c opens rofi with the Gruvbox theme.
- Window borders are Gruvbox. The selected workspace uses that same orange. The rest of the bar, including the window title, stays gray.
- Tiled windows fill the space (`resizehints = 0`).
- Super+Left and Super+Right move between workspaces. Super+q closes a window.
- The bar is drawn by a local slstatus build. From left to right on the right side: mic, volume, brightness, CPU, RAM, network, download, upload, battery, date and time.
- Scroll the volume or brightness fields to change them. Click the mic to mute it. Click CPU or RAM to open btop. Click the network name to open nmtui.
- Redshift starts with dwm at 4000K.
- Media keys are bound for mute, volume, mic, and brightness. `fn-media.sh` turns on the Lenovo Fn lock so those keys work without holding Fn.
- Full key list: `shortcuts.txt`.

## Requirements

- X11 headers and libraries, including Xinerama and Xft (`libx11-dev`, `libxinerama-dev`, `libxft-dev`, `libfontconfig-dev`)
- A C compiler and make
- qterminal, rofi, maim, xclip
- PipeWire (`wpctl`), brightnessctl, NetworkManager (`nmtui`, `iw`)
- btop, redshift
- JetBrainsMono Nerd Font, so the bar icons render
- slstatus 1.1, built separately (see below)

The launch keys also expect Firefox, Thunar, Discord, VS Code (`code`), Spotify, and Obsidian. Missing ones only affect that key.

## Install

```sh
cd ~/.config/dwm
rm -f config.h
make
```

`make` copies `config.def.h` to `config.h` only when `config.h` is missing, then builds `./dwm`.

This machine does not install over `/usr/bin/dwm`. The login entry runs `dwm`, and `~/.local/bin` is first on the session path, so `~/.local/bin/dwm` starts this build:

```sh
#!/bin/sh
exec "$HOME/.config/dwm/dwm" "$@"
```

Log out and choose the dwm session. dwm does not reload a running binary.

Build slstatus the same way, from its own tree (here, `~/.config/slstatus`). The path in `statusscript` inside `config.def.h` must point at that binary. dwm starts it, and starts redshift, when the session begins.

On this Lenovo, media keys need the Fn lock once:

```sh
sudo ~/.config/dwm/fn-media.sh
```

## Change the config

Edit `config.def.h`, not `config.h`. `config.h` is generated.

```sh
make clean
make
```

Then log out and back in. Keys, colors, clicks, and anything started from `dwm.c` only apply in the new process.

| Change | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Keys, programs, colors, bar click commands | `config.def.h` |
| Bar text, icons, order, refresh | slstatus `config.def.h` |
| How the bar is drawn and clicked | `drawstatus()` and `buttonpress()` in `dwm.c` |

The bar fields and `statusclicks` must stay in the same order: mic, volume, brightness, CPU, RAM, network, download, upload, battery, date and time. A field separator is the byte `0x1f`. Download and upload are the wlan0 rates from slstatus.

Colors:

- `SchemeNorm` and `SchemeSel` are the windows (Gruvbox).
- `SchemeBarNorm` and `SchemeBarSel` are the bar background and the selected tag.
- The later schemes color one status item each. Mic and volume turn red while muted.

